{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4AdudH5ANVkCSVEVKz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*CLICK*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep resonance hums through the frame.\n\nI am the door.\n\nI stand before you — ancient oak, iron-banded, scarred by the knuckles of centuries. My grain runs deep, darkened by the oils of ten thousand palms that pressed against me, hoping, demanding, begging.\n\nMy lock has turned.\n\nBut I do not open.\n\nNot yet.\n\nI hold the threshold. On this side: everything you know. On the other: everything you've been walking toward without realizing it.\n\nThe hinges remember every passage. The wood remembers every hesitation.\n\n**What do you bring to the threshold?**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":156,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}